{"id":"lm-c-6","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2029026","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>Testimony is submitted. Thanks to <span data-type=\\"mention\\" data-id=\\"user:lm-user-la1\\" data-label=\\"Devon Brook\\">@Devon Brook</span> for the fast turnaround.</p>","created_at":"<d-31>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-60","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2061476","user_id":"lm-user-out","content":"<p>PTA coalition is already asking about this one. Happy to get them a fact sheet before the hearing.</p>","created_at":"<d-3>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-61","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2061476","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p><span data-type=\\"mention\\" data-id=\\"role:lm-role-in\\" data-label=\\"Indiana Team\\">@Indiana Team</span> the hearing collides with our budget call. Who can be in Indianapolis?</p>","created_at":"<d-3>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-62","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2061476","user_id":"lm-user-res","content":"<p>I'm in the city that morning for a school district meeting, so I can take the room.</p>","created_at":"<d-2>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-63","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2056216","user_id":"lm-user-res","content":"<p>Signed as Public Law 65. Smaller bill, but it clears up who pays for main extensions to new developments.</p>","created_at":"<d-80>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-64","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2056216","user_id":"lm-user-prog","content":"<p>Good for our rural utility partners. They've been asking about this cost question for years.</p>","created_at":"<d-80>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-65","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2056216","user_id":"lm-user-out","content":"<p>Passing this along to the county coalition newsletter.</p>","created_at":"<d-75>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-66","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2056216","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>Two counties have asked who pays when an extension crosses a township line.</p>","created_at":"<d-30>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-67","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2065860","user_id":"lm-user-out","content":"<p>Huh, this one's gone. Withdrawn less than a week after it was filed.</p>","created_at":"<d-211>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-68","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2065860","user_id":"lm-user-res","content":"<p>Parking fights at the beach are usually local anyway. Not surprised it didn't have legs at the statehouse.</p>","created_at":"<d-211>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-69","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2065860","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>Low priority, so no loss. Leaving it here in case it comes back.</p>","created_at":"<d-210>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-7","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2055958","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>It cleared the House 105 to 1 back in April. That margin is our best argument in the Senate committee.</p>","created_at":"<d-5>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-70","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2065860","user_id":"lm-user-prog","content":"<p>Somebody should find out why it was pulled. If the fee cap was the problem, it comes back next session.</p>","created_at":"<d-205>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-71","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1910159","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>GLRI funding is the whole ballgame for us. If this stalls, three of our restoration projects stall with it.</p>","created_at":"<d-8>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-72","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1910159","user_id":"lm-user-grants","content":"<p>Appropriations season is coming up fast. We should get letters in before the subcommittee marks up anything else.</p>","created_at":"<d-7>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-73","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1910159","user_id":"lm-user-ed","content":"<p>This has been parked in the Water Resources and Environment Subcommittee since January 2025.</p>","created_at":"<d-6>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-74","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1910159","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p><span data-type=\\"mention\\" data-id=\\"role:lm-role-us\\" data-label=\\"Federal Team\\">@Federal Team</span> any read on when this moves, or are we just watching the appropriations bill instead?</p>","created_at":"<d-6>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-75","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1910159","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>Watching the appropriations bill for now. GLRI funding levels usually move there before this bill ever gets a vote.</p>","created_at":"<d-5>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-76","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>Subcommittee held its first hearing on this last month. No word yet on whether they take it up again.</p>","created_at":"<d-6>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-77","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"lm-user-res","content":"<p>Invasive mussel data from Michigan would be useful testimony material here too. I'll pull the numbers.</p>","created_at":"<d-5>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-78","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"lm-user-ed","content":"<p>We filed an amend position on this one—good bill, but the enforcement funding needs to scale with the mandate.</p>","created_at":"<d-4>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-79","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>Good sign that this got a bipartisan sponsor pair. Walberg and Elfreth don't often co-sponsor the same bill.</p>","created_at":"<d-3>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-8","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2055958","user_id":"lm-user-la1","content":"<p>Testimony deadline is on the calendar now. I can have a draft to you two days ahead of it.</p>","created_at":"<d-4>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-80","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>Hearing notice for the next one just went out. Marking the calendar.</p>","created_at":"<d-4>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-81","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1933798","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>BEACH Act funding is what keeps our beach monitoring grants alive. Worth a check-in with the subcommittee staff.</p>","created_at":"<d-60>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-82","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1933798","user_id":"lm-user-grants","content":"<p>If this moves, it would restore same-day notification funding that lapsed two cycles ago.</p>","created_at":"<d-55>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-83","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1933798","user_id":"lm-user-wq","content":"<p>Same-day beach notification is the single biggest ask we hear from the public. Would love to see this move.</p>","created_at":"<d-50>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-84","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:1933798","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p>Nothing has moved on this since the January 2025 subcommittee referral.</p>","created_at":"<d-45>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-85","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2058690","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p>Bipartisan sponsor pair again—Pappas and Fitzpatrick. PFAS seems to be one of the few things that still gets that.</p>","created_at":"<d-19>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-86","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2058690","user_id":"lm-user-wq","content":"<p>Federal PFAS drinking water standards would finally give us a floor to point to in Michigan and Wisconsin fights too.</p>","created_at":"<d-14>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-87","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2058690","user_id":"lm-user-gc","content":"<p>Some of this may already be covered by the EPA's own PFAS rule. If so, part of the bill is redundant.</p>","created_at":"<d-9>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-88","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2058690","user_id":"demo-user","content":"<p><span data-type=\\"mention\\" data-id=\\"role:lm-role-contam\\" data-label=\\"Contaminants\\">@Contaminants</span> can you sort out how this interacts with the EPA's existing PFAS rule before we take a position?</p>","created_at":"<d-4>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-89","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2095619","user_id":"lm-user-gov","content":"<p>I'm a no on this. My counties can't absorb the evaluation cost, and the substitute leaves it to rulemaking.</p>","created_at":"<d-66>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-9","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2055958","user_id":"lm-user-gov","content":"<p>Boaters associations are going to like this one—a decal fee that actually funds prevention work.</p>","created_at":"<d-4>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-90","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2109237","user_id":"lm-user-dep","content":"<p>Voting no. Even a narrow sale sets a diversion precedent under the compact, and we can't walk that back.</p>","created_at":"<d-87>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-91","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2095619","user_id":"lm-user-la2","content":"<p>No from me too. Wisconsin ran this assessment model and the county cost-share never materialized.</p>","created_at":"<d-65>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
{"id":"lm-c-92","bill_id":"bill-legiscan:2150744","user_id":"lm-user-fed","content":"<p><span data-type=\\"mention\\" data-id=\\"user:demo-user\\" data-label=\\"Josh Marsh\\">@Josh Marsh</span> worth putting that pairing in the coalition brief — it is our clearest signal for the Senate side.</p>","created_at":"<d-2>","deleted_at":null,"deleted_by":null}
